+---
+id: dl-005-createpatch-semantics-minimal-recursive-diff-non-mutating
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch semantics: minimal recursive diff, non-mutating"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two document versions, as a JSON Patch (RFC 6902).
+
+## Decision
+
+- `createPatch(from, to)` walks both documents: objects member by member (remove, recurse, add), arrays
+  element by element after skipping the common leading and trailing elements, so an insertion or removal
+  does not rewrite what follows. Different types or differing scalars give a `replace`; the root uses the
+  empty path.
+- Only `add`, `remove` and `replace` are emitted; no `move`/`copy` detection, which keeps the output
+  predictable and deterministic (key order of the inputs, no heuristics).
+- Array removals are emitted from the highest index down so earlier indices stay valid.
+- Keys are escaped per RFC 6901; values are `structuredClone`d, so inputs are never mutated or aliased.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The patch is correct and small for localized changes but not guaranteed to be the shortest possible: a
+reordered array or a moved subtree appears as replacements, not moves.
